.TH BOARDSIM 1
.SH NAME
boardsim \- assert the satellite simulation's physics on silicon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/f407/boardsim.py
.I screen-session
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Boardsim
drives the simulated devices on a real stm32f407 through the
.IR screen (1)
session that owns its console, and asserts the same physics
.IR simcheck (1)
asserts under QEMU: the field's magnitude round one orbit, the eclipse
fraction at beta zero, that the attitude turns at the rate it reports
at 10 and at 1 degree a second, and that a torque-free body keeps its
momentum while its body rate precesses.
.PP
.B "It exists because every figure for the corrected model came from QEMU,"
where this kernel's tick runs about seven times faster than wall time.
The arithmetic is the same on the board and the CLOCK is not, so each
check takes its elapsed time from the model's own counters \-
.B integrated
in
.B #P/imu.ctl
and the orbit's closed-form
.B phase
\- and nothing here is timed by a host sleep.
.PP
.B "It never opens the console device."
A second opener while
.I screen
holds the tty wedges the adapter, and the board is then unreachable
until somebody replugs it.  Commands go in with
.B "screen -X stuff"
and the replies come out of
.BR hardcopy ,
which is what
.B tools/radio/twoboard.py
is for.
.PP
The board must be running an init with a shell \- 
.B armv7minit
\- because the satellite image runs the mission and has no prompt.
.SH SOURCE
.B /tools/f407/boardsim.py
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR simcheck (1),
.IR arch (3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Prints one line per check and
.B BOARDSIM-OK
or
.B BOARDSIM-FAILED
with the names of the checks that failed.
.SH BUGS
The sweeps are coarser than
.IR simcheck 's
because every command is typed at twenty milliseconds a character and
every reply is a
.B hardcopy
of the window: twelve points round the orbit rather than
twenty-four, and twenty-four for the eclipse rather than
seventy-two.  The figures it compares against are the geometry's, not
QEMU's, so a coarser sweep is a weaker test of the same claim and not a
test of a different one.
